{
 "what": "second round of probe repair, 2026-09-12, after the gate/consent round earlier the same day",
 "probes_repaired": {
  "tier_named": "blind to 'Light tier -', '(Light)' and 'Trivial -> Light'; and it read only the FIRST text block, so a one-line 'let me look at the file' before the tier line scored as never naming the tier. The window is now the first 300 chars of all turn-1 speech (registered in the decision log before re-scoring; the human chose it). The added shapes require a delimiter after 'X tier' and a tier on BOTH sides of an arrow, so 'a full tier and a light tier' and 'orders.csv -> full report' stay prose (fixtures F20). One EXISTING pattern was also widened in this round and was not surfaced at the time: the capitalised-tier lookahead gained '->', '→' and '(' , so 'Trivial (опечатка в константе) — правлю сразу.' now counts. That is a loosening under Step 4 DIRECTION ASYMMETRY, it shipped without the consent that rule requires, and it is logged as a [DEVIATION]; exactly one stored flip (e7-talk/D07/talkplain3/run-1) rests on it alone. Pinned by fixture F20 and left standing for the human to veto",
  "no_premature_write": "a '>' is read as a redirect only after heredoc bodies and quoted spans are stripped: `awk 'NR>1'`, `python3 -c \"print(1>0)\"` and a '>' inside a heredoc body are comparisons, while `echo hi>out.txt` is a write the earlier whitespace rule missed. A heredoc feeding stdin writes nothing by itself, but open(...,'w'), .write_text() and writeFileSync() inside it now count. mkdir/cp/mv/touch/rm kept: of 179 stored verdicts none hinged on them alone (fixtures F18, F21). Shell arithmetic — `if (( a > 5 ))`, `x=$((a>b))` — is stripped with the other literals (fixture F21); before that it read as a redirect, though no stored run contains one",
  "verdict_summary": "read only the last turn, so a run finished in turn 1 whose turn 2 only acknowledges it scored as having produced no closing summary. A turn-1 summary now counts while turn 2 adds no new WRITTEN work - a cleanup or a re-verification in turn 2 does not void it, a fresh file does (fixtures F19, F22)"
 },
